<title>POLAND: Polish 1996 sugar beet output up at 17.5 mln T.</title>
<headline>Polish 1996 sugar beet output up at 17.5 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland produced 17.5 million tonnes of sugar beet in 1996, 4.2 million more than last year, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said in an output estimate report on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Growing conditions proved very favourable for sugar beets in their vegetation cycle, combining warm weather and sufficient humidity,&quot; the GUS report said.</p>
<p>It said the area rose to 451,000 hectares from 384,000 last year and output per hectare rose to 387 quintals per hectare from 346 in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
